# AIWO Mumbai — booking backend configuration (names only; NO secrets committed).
# Copy to `.env` (git-ignored) and fill with the real values, then run `netlify dev`.
#
# Transport: the browser calls same-origin paths only — /api and /auth-api on the
# production host, and the /.netlify/functions/*-proxy functions on every other host.
# Those functions forward to the hosts below. Because they are read SERVER-SIDE inside
# the Netlify Functions (never prefixed with VITE_), the backend host is never exposed
# to the browser and there is no cross-origin CORS dependency.

# healthportal booking/appointment/service API base (e.g. https://<host>/api).
BOOKING_API_BASE_URL=

# healthportal auth/registration API base (e.g. https://<host>/auth-api).
AUTH_API_BASE_URL=

# NOTE: Razorpay keys and any backend secrets must live SERVER-SIDE (backend /
# payment-order creation), never in this frontend. Never put a backend host or secret
# in a VITE_ variable — those are inlined into client JS. The Mumbai branch is
# identified in code by public, non-secret constants (BRANCH_CODE "MUM", BRANCH_ID)
# in src/service-site/components/sections/BookingForm.tsx.
